10^6], SIX orders of magnitude (values 0.7794, 0.7648, 0.7759, 0.7807, 0.7780, 0.7774; mean 0.7760, std 0.0055). Greedy at N=10^6: primes 990, random 1053; prime integrality gap 1.273. STRUCTURAL CONCLUSION: the Ulam-spiral LP gives a fractional structural fact about primes (HL slope-+/-1 diagonals carry stable 70% LP weight), but this does NOT translate to integer algorithmic compression. Slot 5 should close the thread B-NEGATIVE on integer-cover grounds OR pursue asymptotic LP-gap proof for theoretical interest (5-orders-of-magnitude stability is strong evidence for asymptotic LP gap proof being viable). B grade (substantive partial-positive empirical fact, structural refinement of slot 3 from B+ to B because the integer claim is asymptotically vanishing, but LP claim strengthened by N=3*10^5 confirmation).
