    5675	### D43 — Hairer regularity structures / KPZ universality of the prime counting error term `π(x) − Li(x)`  [PARTIAL CLOSURE S157, KPZ-grid Hölder + Tracy-Widom β=2 sub-frame closed; D43.b/D43.c sub-frames OPEN]
    5676	
    5677	**Question:** the explicit formula gives
    5678	`π(x) − Li(x) = -\sum_ρ Li(x^ρ) + O(\log x)` summed over non-trivial
    5679	ζ-zeros. Treating `D(x) := (π(x) − Li(x)) \log x / \sqrt{x}` as a
    5680	*random function of x* on the natural CLT scale, all project
    5681	measurements have tested *Gaussian / Wigner semicircle* universality
    5682	(C5 Stein CLOSED, C7 FHK CLOSED, S74 free cumulants CLOSED, GUE pair
    5683	correlation E3.1). Question: does `D(x)` viewed as a stochastic
    5684	process on `x ∈ [1, X]` and rescaled by `t^{1/3}` (KPZ scale) instead
    5685	of `\sqrt{t}` (CLT scale) fall into the **Kardar-Parisi-Zhang
    5686	universality class** with Tracy-Widom β=2 fluctuations? KPZ governs
    5687	interface-growth fluctuations in nonlinear stochastic systems; its
    5688	limit law `F_2` (Tracy-Widom β=2) shares the *distribution* with GUE
    5689	largest eigenvalue, but the **scaling exponent is different**: KPZ
    5690	has `t^{1/3}` while GUE has `\sqrt{t}`. A KPZ-type fluctuation in
    5691	`π(x) - Li(x)` at the `x^{1/3}` scale would constitute a NEW
    5692	universality class for the prime counting error term, orthogonal to
    5693	the project's `\sqrt{x}/\log x`-scale Gaussian battery.
    5694	
    5695	**Why frontier:** Hairer 2014 *Inventiones* (Fields Medal) gave the
    5696	first rigorous theory of singular SPDE limits, establishing the KPZ
    5697	universality class with `t^{1/3}` scaling and Tracy-Widom β=2 limit
    5698	for a wide universality class of nonlinear interface-growth processes.
