    1	"""
    2	ATTACK_VECTORS §C2 — Higher-order arithmetic corrections (Conrey-Snaith).
    3	
    4	Test orders 4, 5, 6 of zeta-zero n-correlations at N=8000.
    5	Three complementary probes:
    6	
    7	  (A) k-th nearest-neighbor spacing distributions P_k(s) for k=0..5.
    8	      P_k probes the (k+2)-point correlation directly (P_5 sees orders
    9	      up to 7-point clusters). Strong-statistics 1D histograms.
    10	
    11	  (B) Higher cumulants kappa_n(L) of zero counts in disjoint windows
    12	      for n=2..6 at L in {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128}. kappa_n is
    13	      sensitive to n-point correlations; for a GUE DPP the closed form
    14	      is
    15	
    16	         log det(I + (e^t - 1) K_L) = sum_n kappa_n(L) t^n / n!
    17	
    18	      with sine-kernel K(x, y) = sin(pi (x-y)) / (pi (x-y)).
    19	
    20	  (C) Equally-spaced n-tuple density R_n(0, s, 2s, ..., (n-1)s) for
    21	      n=4, 5, 6, swept over s in [0.5, 5]. GUE prediction:
    22	          R_n(s_1,...,s_n) = det[K(s_i - s_j)]_{i,j}.
    23	
    24	For each test:
    25	  - Empirical from the N=8000 unfolded zeta zeros.
    26	  - GUE Monte Carlo: eigenvalues of a single N=8000 GUE matrix
    27	    (Hermitian-Wigner; central bulk extracted, unfolded by semicircle).
    28	  - Gap-shuffled null: K=20 seeds preserving the gap-marginal
    29	    (kills higher-order correlations beyond 1-spacing).
