    22:| Pfaffian / α-determinantal point process structure of ζ zeros at order n=4 (ATTACK_VECTORS §C6) | FAIL | E | First project measurement of GOE/GSE Pfaffian and Vere-Jones α-DPP point-process models on ζ-zero R_4 at order n=4 (8000 unfolded zeros, 96 random non-equally-spaced 4-tuples in [0.5, 6.0], window-counting at tol=0.20). **B-grade structural negative on Pfaffian:** χ²/dof discrimination (dof=96, per-tuple SE=0.135 from GUE-MC batches) gives ζ vs sine-kernel det theory **0.96** (perfect fit), ζ vs GUE-MC pool **1.24**, ζ vs GOE-MC pool **1.99** (rejects GOE), ζ vs GSE-MC pool **3.11** (strongly rejects GSE). Decisive structural rejection: GOE Pfaffian and GSE Pfaffian models do NOT fit ζ-zero R_4 at order 4, while sine-kernel determinantal model fits within noise. **B+ partial-positive on α-DPP shift:** α-determinant scan over α ∈ [−1.5, −0.5] at Δα=0.025 finds α\*(zeta) = **−1.10** with L2\* = 0.114 vs L2(α=−1) = 0.118 (ΔL2 = 0.0045); tuple-bootstrap (200 resamples) 95% CI [−1.150, −1.049] formally excludes α=−1. **Critical bias control:** 16 independent matched-size 8000-eigenvalue GUE-MC trials with same 96 tuples + same α-DPP scan: α\* mean = **−1.013**, std = 0.035, 0/16 trials at α\* ≤ −1.10. ζ at α\* = −1.10 is **z ≈ −2.5σ** below GUE-MC distribution (parametric one-sided p = 0.007; non-parametric Laplace p = 0.059). The α-DPP shift is suggestive but does NOT meet the 5σ A-grade bar. Closure mode E because Pfaffian/α-DPP discrimination at order 4 reduces to standard sine-kernel determinantal model at the finite-N detection floor (analogous to §C1/S71 and §C2/S123 closures sharing the same 1/L²~10⁻³ noise barrier). Cross-domain ingredient (Pfaffian point processes, Vere-Jones α-DPP) performed real work; first project use of α-determinantal generalisation. Refines **EDGE E7.1** from "DPP-typical at orders 4-6" to "DPP-typical AND not GOE/GSE Pfaffian-typical at order 4 (χ²/dof 1.99 / 3.11 rejection)" + "α-DPP best-fit α\* = −1.10 ± ~0.04 with 2.5σ shift from GUE-MC matched-size distribution, suggestive non-decisive partial-positive". Successor sub-frames OPEN: **C6.b** Odlyzko γ ≥ 10⁶ extension (would push 2.5σ to 5σ if α\* shift is real), **C6.c** denser tuple sampling at fixed N=8000. Cross-domain refs: Borodin 2009 *Encyclopaedia Math. Sci.* 152 = arXiv:0911.1153 §2.4-2.6; Soshnikov 2000 *Russ. Math. Surv.* 55 = arXiv:math/0002099 §3; Vere-Jones 1997 *NZ J. Math.* 26 (α-permanent); Mehta 2004 *Random Matrices* §6 (GOE/GSE Pfaffian formulas). Promotes CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §3 row "Pfaffian / α-determinantal point processes" PROPOSED → USED-E. See `experiments/analytic/zeta_structure/c6_pfaffian_alpha_dpp_n4/`. | 489 |
    718:| Levin universal search on delta(n) with explicit 11-token RPN DSL through length 8 | FAIL | I | Refines line 211 (S7). Enumerated all type-correct RPN programs of length <=8 over the alphabet {n, 0..3, +, -, *, //, %, L (bit_length), S (isqrt)} = 11 tokens (3.6M programs) and scored against delta(1..50). Best partial fit isqrt(n-1) - n//2 matches delta(1..9) by coincidence and breaks at n=10 (delta(10)=0 vs program output -2). Best non-coincidence match length 7 covers only 5/50. Length 8 = ~28 program-bits, two orders of magnitude below the >=280 information bits delta(1..50) carries (Shannon ratio 0.84 from line 595, Kt 5.58 bits/value from line 489). Length 9: ~35M programs; length 10: ~350M; length 12: ~35B (intractable). Concrete description-length floor on delta in this DSL. See experiments/proposals/levin_search_delta.py | 49 |
    786:| §A5 ATTACK_VECTORS — Maynard 2015 multidimensional sieve weight w(n) = (Σ_{d_i\|n+h_i, gcd=1, ∏d_i≤R} μ(d_1)…μ(d_k) F(log d_i/log R))^2 as TC^0 primality witness (cross-domain: Maynard 2015 *Annals* 181 / Polymath8b 2014 / Pascadi 2025) | FAIL | E | Wild-swing attack S116 on the most refined explicit prime-detection sieve in modern analytic NT, framed as: is `w(n) > τ*` a pointwise primality witness AND is w(n) polylog-evaluable, so that PRIMES ∈ TC⁰ unconditionally? Implementation: `experiments/sieve/maynard_weight_pointwise/`. k=3, H=admissible {0,2,6} (also tested {0,4,6} and {0,2,6,8,12}); F ∈ {(1-Σx_i)^2 GPY, (1-Σx_i) linear, constant=1, Maynard-symmetric (1-Σx)^2(1+0.5Σx+2Σx_ix_j)}; θ ∈ {0.10,0.15,0.20,0.25,0.30,0.35,0.40} (R = N^θ); N ∈ {10^4, 10^4.5, 10^5, 10^5.5, 10^6}. **Pre-registered targets**: A-grade requires AUC restricted to odd n ≥ 0.95 AND mean ops/eval = polylog(N). Both fail. **Pointwise-AUC table (selberg_gpy F)**: at θ ≤ 0.20 with R<6, AUC_all ranges 0.84–0.90 — but stratification by parity reveals that 0.22 of the AUC is *parity detection* (H={0,2,6} share parity ⇒ even n window has zero primes). AUC restricted to odd n is in [0.66, 0.69] across all θ. Best F1 = 0.62 with selberg_gpy. The maynard_sym F (with 2-parameter symmetric correction) is no better — eigenvalue ratio M_3/I_3 = 1.515 controls aggregate, not pointwise. **Aggregate-positivity replicated**: max ratio Σw(n)χ_P(n+h_i)/Σw(n) = 0.094–0.212 across θ — Maynard's theorem holds at finite N. The empirical pointwise/aggregate gap is DIRECTLY the structural fact that `Σ w·χ_P > c·Σ w` does NOT propagate to single-n separation. **Op-count scaling**: mean coprime simplex tuples ∝ N^α for α ∈ {0.10, 0.11, 0.12} at θ ∈ {0.20, 0.30, 0.40} on N ∈ [10^4, 10^6] — sub-θ but POSITIVE; not polylog. Worst-case (p99) tuple count grows with same exponent. Divisor enumeration up to R = N^θ is the fundamental sub-routine and reduces to growing-dim modular powering — exactly E5.3. **Mechanism for closure mode E**: Maynard's main theorem is `Σ w·χ_P ≥ c·Σ w` (averaged); pointwise content of w(n) is bounded by aggregate-vs-pointwise loss factor that depends on the F-eigenvalue ratio, not on F-shape. Empirical AUC_oddN ≤ 0.69 across all θ confirms this loss is irreducible; maynard_sym attempt did not improve over selberg_gpy. **Refines E6.7 (sieve pebbling)** by closing the most refined Selberg-sieve descendant; **reduces to E5.3 (MPOW)** via divisor-enumeration cost; **closes the project's only open problem (PRIMES in TC⁰) along the sieve-route attack family**, completing the four-family closure {AKS-modulus E7.10, Brandt MKtP E5.8, convergence-acceleration E7.11, **Maynard sieve E7.14**}. **Cross-domain ingredient (multidim GPY-Maynard sieve) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded PROPOSED → USED E with edge E7.14. **Adds EDGE E7.14**: Maynard 2015 multidim weight is aggregate-not-pointwise (AUC_oddN ∈ [0.66, 0.69]) AND requires Ω(N^{θ-o(1)}) divisor-enumeration cost per single n (sub-poly, not polylog) for any θ > 0 with non-trivial weight. Cites E6.7, E5.3, E7.10. Cross-domain refs: Maynard 2015 *Annals* 181:383 = arXiv:1311.4600; Polymath8b 2014 arXiv:1407.4897; Pascadi 2025 (E3.12). See experiments/sieve/maynard_weight_pointwise/maynard_weight_pointwise_results.md. | 116 |
